// Grid 10 by 6, the designer's 500 by 300 pixel image in units of 50. Quarters split at the
// center. The white pile stands on the top edge from 1 to 9 and reaches the bottom edge, 6.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Transsex flag"
  designer "beyond-mogai-pride-flags (Tumblr), mod a-p"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2020-02-14"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20241207085605/https://beyond-mogai-pride-flags.tumblr.com/post/190825906610/transex-pride-flag"
  source "https://lgbtqia.wiki/wiki/Transsex"
  note "Defining source: the post 'Transex Pride Flag' by beyond-mogai-pride-flags, posted by the blog on Friday 14 February 2020 and signed by mod a-p, read at the Wayback Machine snapshot above. It defines transex (transsex, transexed or transsexed) as a sex label, close to transsexual and transgender but not the same, and an umbrella for labels such as transgenital and transgonadal. It gives no color meanings or values."
  note "Construction and colors are read from the post's image (500 by 300 PNG, 5:3): quartered blue and pink, blue in the upper hoist and lower fly, with a white triangle standing on the top edge from 50 to 450 pixels and its point at the middle of the bottom edge. Colors: blue #00a2e8, white #ffffff, and two pinks, #ffa8be in the upper fly and #ffaec9 in the lower hoist. The two pinks are kept as drawn, though the difference may not be intended. This is my sampling, not hex the designer gave."
  note "Pride-Flags' DeviantArt 'Transsexual (1)' of 22 August 2015 is a different, older flag: seven pink and blue stripes parted by white, with a lavender male-and-female symbol near the hoist, after Johnathan Andrew's 1999 transgender flag. It is not this flag."
}
palette {
  blue "#00a2e8"
  pink "#ffa8be"
  light-pink "#ffaec9"
  white "#ffffff"
}
proportion hoist=6 fly=10

quarters blue pink light-pink blue

pile white {
  from top
  base 1 9
  depth 6
}
